      ],
      "observations": [
        "Helper return values propagate failures with Context/Result. Callers consume the Result using ? or test-local expect; no success default is introduced.",
        "Original payload, signature, nonce, authority, dispatch-count and rejection assertions remain.",
        "Error definitions inspected are standard error types compatible with anyhow Context. hepta-memory includes the needed dev dependency.",
        "Existing clippy configuration permits expect inside test bodies; this change does not add allow attributes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "SQLite migration and schema fixtures",
      "status": "source_review_pass",
      "files": [
        "codex-rs/hepta-automation/src/migration_convergence_tests.rs",
        "codex-rs/hepta-memory/src/cognitive_schema_tests.rs"
      ],
      "observations": [
        "Direct in-memory SqlitePool connections are replaced with the existing SqliteConfig durable-pool API and a private temporary database.",
        "historical_pool returns both TempDir and pool. All callers bind the TempDir guard; it remains alive through migration, VACUUM INTO and pool.close.",
        "SqliteConfig opens the connection with WAL/FULL/foreign keys but does not run owner migrations; the historical fixtures still explicitly build their original migration cuts.",
        "The VACUUM destination is separately retained. Source pool is closed before the real owner is opened. Checksum, branch-convergence, repeated-restart and corrupt-history assertions remain.",
        "The schema oracle is still derived from compiled migrations in a fresh database; tampered trigger rejection remains."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Core FIFO event receiver",
      "status": "source_review_pass_integration_pending",
      "files": [
        "codex-rs/core/src/tasks/mod.rs",
        "codex-rs/core/src/tasks/terminal_event_barrier_tests.rs"
      ],
      "observations": [
        "A private one-permit Tokio semaphore serializes channel receive and synchronous sidecar pairing across concurrent consumers.",
        "No data mutex guard is held over channel await. Cancellation and receive failure release the permit through RAII.",
        "There is no suspension point between a successful event receive and sidecar pairing. Cancelling a pending async-channel receive does not consume an event.",
        "Existing publisher ordering and completion-owner identity remain unchanged.",
        "New actual-Session tests cover reused-turn FIFO pairing with reverse polling order, queued and active receiver cancellation, and consecutive closed-channel errors.",
        "Review caught Event lacking PartialEq. Three comparisons now serialize and compare complete Event objects without changing the production Event type."
      ],
      "not_executed": [
        "Full codex-core compilation",
        "New actual-Session receiver tests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Pure Rust YAML migration",
      "status": "actual_source_isolated_tests_pass_owner_ci_pending",
      "observations": [
        "Four production owners no longer reference serde_yaml. External-agent migration reuses the core-plugins compatibility reader instead of adding another direct parser dependency.",
        "The parser pins YAML boolean interpretation and treats merge keys as ordinary keys. The dynamic migration reader retains ordered scalar fields, unsupported values and non-string-key handling.",
        "Compatibility adjustments cover tagged mapping/key transparency, application-tagged values, aliases retaining definition spelling, leading-zero strings, finite and non-finite numeric spelling, and 64-bit integer range.",
        "Existing skilled frontmatter repair tests execute against the actual edited parser source, not a mirrored parser implementation.",
        "The finite differential corpus establishes compatibility for its 48 documents only; it is not a proof for all possible YAML inputs."
      ]
    },
